# Kconfig symbols for the Skree Custom module (repo root).
# zephyr/module.yml points Zephyr here with `build: kconfig: Kconfig`.

config SKREE_LINK_WATCHDOG
    bool "Re-time the split link when trackball reports drop to half rate"
    default y
    depends on ZMK_SPLIT_ROLE_CENTRAL && ZMK_BLE
    help
      The left half runs two 7.5 ms Bluetooth links on one radio: it is a
      peripheral to the host and the central to the right half. When the two
      links' connection events overlap, the radio serves only one per slot, so
      the trackball reports from the right half arrive in pairs every other
      event (~15 ms) and the pointer stutters.

      This watchdog watches the arrival times of the split trackball reports
      and, when more than 35% of a 40-report window arrives bunched together,
      changes the split link's connection interval (8.75 ms, then 7.5 ms again
      about 150 ms later) so the events land in a different slot relative to
      the host link. Nothing runs while the ball is idle.

      Say n to leave the link timing entirely to ZMK.
